[s0l0!-header][h1]Default Parameters in ES6[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

In ES6, we can put the default values right in the signature of the functions.
[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="js" codeId="1438"]function test(a, [b]b = 3[/b], [b]c = 42[/b]) {
  return a + b + c;
}
console.log(test(5)); //50[/code]
And here's an example of an arrow function with default parameters:[code format="js" ]const test = (a, [b]b = 3[/b], [b]c = 42[/b]) => {
  return a + b + c;
}
console.log(test(5)); //50 [/code]
[note]Default value expressions are evaluated at function call time from left to right. This also means that default expressions can use the values of previously-filled parameters.[/note]

